{{also|Bremsstrahlung}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Bremsstrahlung||braking or deceleration radiation}}, which had been coined in German by {{w|Arnold Sommerfeld}} from {{compound|de|Bremse|t1=a brake|Strahlung|t2=radiation|nocat=1}} in 1909, and was first used in English by {{w|Arthur Edward Ruark}} and {{w|Harold Urey}} in 1930.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɹɛm.ʃtrɑ.ləŋ/|/ˈbɹɛms.ʃtrɑ.ləŋ/|/ˈbɹɛm.strɑ.ləŋ/|/-lʊŋ/|/-lʌŋ/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[electromagnetic radiation]] produced by the [[deceleration]] of a [[charged]] [[particle]], such as an [[electron]], when it is [[deflect]]ed by another charged particle, such as an [[atomic nucleus]].

